  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 245 PM MDT Mon Sep 28 2026\n\nThursday...In the wake of the passing trough aloft, dry northwest \nflow aloft will develop, thus no showers or thunderstorms expected.\nSomewhat cooler based on 700 mb temperature changes.\n\nFriday...West northwest flow aloft strengthens, helping low level \ngradients to increase enough to produce breezy to windy conditions. \nLow and mid levels look too dry to support shower and thunderstorm \ndevelopment.\n\nSaturday...A fast moving positively tilted shortwave trough aloft \nmoves across Nebraska, sending a dry cold front across our counties.\nContinued dry. \n\nSunday...The ridge aloft to our south over Colorado and New Mexico \nwill produce enough convective inhibition to make shower and \nthunderstorm development quite unlikely for our forecast area.\n\nMonday...Non-descript northwest flow aloft continues. There may be \nenough low and middle level moisture to produce isolated to widely \nscattered thunderstorms in the afternoon and evening, but \npinpointing their location will be iffy at best. Another warming \ntrend develops as 700 mb temperatures rise once again.",
